1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:30,000
= kisskh.lv =

2
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:47,056
We're very sorry for the disruption to your travel plans.

3
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:49,256
Thank you for your patience and understanding.

4
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:50,976
No worries.

5
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:54,856
Ms. Zhang, we apologize for the inconvenience to your onward journey.

6
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:56,096
Hello, Ms. Fu.

7
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:58,055
Thank you so much for your assistance today.

8
00:01:58,079 --> 00:02:01,136
Please accept this fruit platter with our compliments.

9
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:02,776
It was my pleasure. You're welcome.

10
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,560
We really appreciate it.

11
00:02:23,639 --> 00:02:24,936
Captain, your coffee.

12
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:26,936
Great. Thanks.

13
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:28,216
Thank you.

14
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:29,496
Yu.

15
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:30,616
Thanks.

16
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:31,896
- Captain Fan.
- Yes?

17
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:36,135
We received word before takeoff that the passenger is out of danger.

18
00:02:36,159 --> 00:02:40,496
Manager Wang also said Mr. Fu is treating the whole crew to dinner.

19
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:43,096
You all worked hard today. A good meal is well deserved.

20
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:45,080
Thank you, Captain Fan.

21
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:53,735
Lei, does that mean our bonus is pretty much in the bag?

22
00:02:53,759 --> 00:02:57,136
Mentor, you were incredible today!

23
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:58,896
When will I ever be as good as you?

24
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,656
You don't want to be like me.

25
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:03,200
The best flight is the one where nothing happens.

26
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:11,720
[Episode 8] [Want to Be My Boyfriend Instead?]

27
00:03:22,639 --> 00:03:24,376
Captain Fan, Ruan.

28
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:26,015
- Come on in.
- I'm waiting for them.

29
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:27,295
I immediately called the purser.

30
00:03:27,319 --> 00:03:28,816
That's when I finally calmed down.

31
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:31,101
- The one who calmed you down was Jiang.
- Mentor.

32
00:03:31,125 --> 00:03:34,976
When it comes to emergencies, Jiang is the one with real experience.

33
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,456
- Alright. Let's go.
- Let's go.

34
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:38,735
This place is so upscale. Will we get enough to eat?

35
00:03:38,759 --> 00:03:40,651
- Hurry up.
- I'm starving.

36
00:03:43,879 --> 00:03:45,840
It's nice and cool.

37
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:48,920
You're here.

38
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:52,496
- Mr. Fu.
- Ruan.

39
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:54,936
You got here early.

40
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:57,096
When pouring his drink, my hands were shaking...

41
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,800
Everyone's here.

42
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:01,921
Come on, grab a seat. Come on.

43
00:04:01,945 --> 00:04:04,735
- We're not late, are we? Let me see...
- No, we were early.

44
00:04:04,759 --> 00:04:05,895
Captain Fan, please.

45
00:04:05,919 --> 00:04:07,256
Sit. Ruan, you too.

46
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:09,016
Sit over here. Come on.

47
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:10,096
Captain Fan. Thank you.

48
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:11,936
Take your seats. Don't be shy.

49
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:13,615
Sit here. Come on.

50
00:04:13,639 --> 00:04:15,136
Here. Come.

51
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:17,256
- Please, go ahead.
- Everyone, please sit down.

52
00:04:17,280 --> 00:04:20,920
Excuse me? We're ready for our food now.

53
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:31,776
Busy. Handle it yourself.

54
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:34,495
Alright. Many people came today.

55
00:04:34,519 --> 00:04:36,376
All dishes are served. Please enjoy.

56
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:38,000
Thank you.

57
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,855
Alright, everyone.

58
00:04:51,879 --> 00:04:56,175
Before we eat, let's have Mr. Fu say a few words, shall we?

59
00:04:56,199 --> 00:04:58,160
- Yes, come on.
- Please.

60
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:03,376
No speeches over dinner.

61
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:04,976
Or it'll feel like a meeting.

62
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,656
Okay then, how about Captain Fan?

63
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:12,000
Good. Captain Fan, please say something for us.

64
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:14,696
I'm not talking either.

65
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:17,256
It'll turn into a coordination meeting.

66
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:18,656
Then.

67
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:20,616
Ms. Jiang, why don't you say something?

68
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:21,656
I'll pass.

69
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:23,576
It'll sound like a briefing. Let's not.

70
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:26,816
Come on, nobody wants to talk? I can't either. That'd be weird.

71
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:30,726
Looks like everyone's tense because I'm here.

72
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:33,816
I don't think you're usually this quiet.

73
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:36,496
Yeah, you folks are usually pretty lively.

74
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:39,680
- Yeah, we're pretty outgoing.
- Yes, very outgoing.

75
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:43,019
I want to say something.

76
00:05:43,043 --> 00:05:45,656
Today was my first flight as the lead attendant.

77
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:49,336
I was already nervous, and when the accident happened, I just froze.

78
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:51,256
I don't feel like I contributed much.

79
00:05:51,280 --> 00:05:52,816
Sit down.

80
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:56,096
While we were doing CPR up front,

81
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:58,696
you were in the back keeping everyone calm and steady.

82
00:05:58,720 --> 00:06:00,336
That was the biggest help.

83
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:04,041
I almost forgot it was your first lead attendant flight.

84
00:06:04,065 --> 00:06:05,215
And all of you.

85
00:06:05,239 --> 00:06:08,416
Everyone did an amazing job today.

86
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:10,136
Your scores will definitely be solid.

87
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:12,400
- Great.
- Good to hear.

88
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,776
I almost forgot.

89
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:19,760
On my first flight as a flight attendant, Jiang was my purser too.

90
00:06:21,276 --> 00:06:25,456
She always sees the best in people and lifts them up.

91
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:30,216
Getting Jiang on your first flight means you're very lucky.

92
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:32,296
You're making me blush.

93
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:34,576
Working with all of you is my honor too.

94
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:35,856
Here's to everyone.

95
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:37,680
Good.

96
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:42,296
I was really panicking today.

97
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:44,606
I was terrified something would go wrong.

98
00:06:44,630 --> 00:06:49,255
Otherwise, we'd surely have been punished.

99
00:06:49,279 --> 00:06:50,295
Come on.

100
00:06:50,319 --> 00:06:51,656
You worked so hard to save her.

101
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:54,496
A commendation letter is definitely coming your way.

102
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:56,576
We really owe that doctor today.

103
00:06:56,600 --> 00:07:00,416
Didn't even get her number to properly thank her.

104
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:03,960
If she hadn't been there, we'd have been in real trouble.

105
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:06,656
Alright, everyone.

106
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:09,579
Let's get our drinks poured, shall we?

107
00:07:09,603 --> 00:07:12,332
Let's all raise a glass to today.

108
00:07:12,356 --> 00:07:16,280
And then we'll have Mr. Fu say the final words.

109
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:21,216
There's only one rule tonight.

110
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:22,415
Eat well.

111
00:07:22,439 --> 00:07:23,880
Drink well.

112
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:26,017
Cheers.

113
00:07:26,041 --> 00:07:27,320
Thank you.

114
00:07:27,960 --> 00:07:30,216
Come on, eat and drink your fill.

115
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:32,096
Eat well, drink well.

116
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:33,336
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

117
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:34,616
To everyone. Enjoy the meal.

118
00:07:34,640 --> 00:07:36,616
Thank you.

119
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:38,856
- Such a great evening.
- Seriously.

120
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:40,096
I feel like eating...

121
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:41,295
Our ride's here. We'll head off.

122
00:07:41,319 --> 00:07:44,175
- Bye.
- Bye.

123
00:07:44,199 --> 00:07:46,376
How are you getting home?

124
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:48,376
Ruan, where do you live? I can give you a lift.

125
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:50,136
No, thank you. I'll take her.

126
00:07:50,160 --> 00:07:51,896
Alright then. I'm off.

127
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:54,615
Actually, it's not that far.

128
00:07:54,639 --> 00:07:56,456
I'd like to walk home.

129
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:59,776
Funny, I was thinking the same thing.

130
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:04,376
Alright then, I'll head off. Stay safe.

131
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:05,896
Yu, come with me.

132
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:07,496
- Bye, mentor.
- Bye.

133
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:09,508
Mr. Fu, Ruan. I'll be going now.

134
00:08:09,532 --> 00:08:11,063
Okay, bye.

135
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:54,640
[Great Michelin. Let's come together someday.] [Almost done here. Where are you?]

136
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:21,080
I thought Jiang was quite lovely today.

137
00:09:22,886 --> 00:09:24,646
How so?

138
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:28,256
I've flown with her a few times before,

139
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:31,936
but I always felt like she had some issue with me.

140
00:09:31,960 --> 00:09:33,336
Today was different.

141
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:37,000
It felt like when we first met.

142
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:43,360
"If only life could be still at the very moment when we met for the first time"?

143
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:47,722
Some first meetings are better left forgotten.

144
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:01,136
Two orders of sea worm rice bowls.

145
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:02,840
Coming right up!

146
00:10:19,769 --> 00:10:22,056
Didn't you get enough to eat tonight?

147
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:25,320
Did anyone at that table look like they ate their fill?

148
00:10:28,586 --> 00:10:33,641
So if I hadn't shown up tonight, everyone would've eaten better?

149
00:10:33,665 --> 00:10:35,256
Mr. Fu,

150
00:10:35,280 --> 00:10:39,200
sometimes you're surprisingly self-aware.

151
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:43,560
Want some?

152
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,529
I suggest you try it.

153
00:10:47,553 --> 00:10:49,433
It's really delicious.

154
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:06,296
So?

155
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:08,496
I've never had it before.

156
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:10,942
But it's not bad.

157
00:11:10,966 --> 00:11:13,486
Stop it.

158
00:11:18,194 --> 00:11:19,674
Today,

159
00:11:19,698 --> 00:11:23,822
nobody in the back knew what was happening in the cockpit.

160
00:11:23,846 --> 00:11:26,016
They all thought it was just another routine landing.

161
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:30,696
But only Yu and I knew how incredible my mentor was up there.

162
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:35,267
I don't think anyone else could've handled it that perfectly.

163
00:11:35,291 --> 00:11:39,828
The craziest part is, after we landed, she was so calm,

164
00:11:39,852 --> 00:11:42,022
like nothing had happened.

165
00:11:42,046 --> 00:11:43,692
Totally unfazed.

166
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:49,696
Your mentor really is something.

167
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:52,216
She's been your instructor for a while now.

168
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:53,496
Do you know her well?

169
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:55,480
Of course I do.

170
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:02,780
I seem to recall that before I came to Hengshi Air, she had a similar heroic moment.

171
00:12:02,804 --> 00:12:05,976
- Do you remember?
- Everyone in the industry knew about it.

172
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:09,896
That's how I first learned about Captain Fan.

173
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:13,136
Do you remember what happened after?

174
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:14,656
After?

175
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:17,836
She became a celebrity captain, then an instructor.

176
00:12:17,860 --> 00:12:19,096
Now she's my mentor.

177
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:20,680
Why?

178
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:24,720
Nothing.

179
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:31,120
I was thinking, people as brilliant as Captain Fan

180
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:35,336
might carry a lot of weight that nobody sees.

181
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:41,056
In other words, maybe the outcome they get doesn't always match what they put in.

182
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:43,826
Isn't that the charm of this profession?

183
00:12:43,850 --> 00:12:48,536
I'm probably not at her level yet, so I can't really feel it.

184
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:51,289
I'll have to earn the left seat of a domestically built aircraft

185
00:12:51,313 --> 00:12:53,513
before I can truly understand.

186
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:04,696
I do have a question for you.

187
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:07,176
If I hadn't offered you double the signing bonus,

188
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:09,416
would you still have chosen Hengshi Air?

189
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:11,336
Let me tell you,

190
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:14,896
Yan An's sitting at Bo'ao Air with double the bonus waiting for me.

191
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:16,696
Take it or leave it.

192
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:18,176
Yan An?

193
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:21,296
But does Yan An have the Z101, that domestically built large aircraft?

194
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:22,456
No.

195
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:24,296
But maybe in a couple of years they will.

196
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:28,256
And does Yan An have Captain Fan as your instructor?

197
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:29,840
No, they don't.

198
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:33,376
So then, Ms. Ruan,

199
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:37,696
don't you think you could go a little easier on me?

200
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:39,680
Have I been hard on you?

201
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:47,856
But seriously, thank you for the double bonus, Mr. Fu.

202
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:52,176
With that, I can save up a bit more

203
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:54,280
and finally buy a place.

204
00:14:00,247 --> 00:14:05,216
I've asked Captain Fan about that.

205
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:08,656
Don't take it the wrong way. Just a standard employee background check.

206
00:14:08,680 --> 00:14:11,360
I know you sold your old house.

207
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:21,135
So the contract is signed.

208
00:14:21,159 --> 00:14:23,840
We'll go through the transfer process next.

209
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:29,976
Can I stay here for a little while longer?

210
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:31,855
- Of course.
- Thank you.

211
00:14:31,879 --> 00:14:33,976
I'll lock up when I leave.

212
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:35,096
- Alright.
- Alright then.

213
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:37,360
We'll be going then, Ms. Ruan.

214
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:13,696
You little troublemaker.

215
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:16,416
Old Ruan! Your wife is picking on me again.

216
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:18,440
Let me see.

217
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:20,616
Look at your messy little face.

218
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:22,136
Don't bother your mom.

219
00:15:22,160 --> 00:15:23,176
Hurry up and eat.

220
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:24,712
You too, eat up.

221
00:15:24,736 --> 00:15:26,096
Breakfast time!

222
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:28,056
I'll make your mom stand in the corner later.

223
00:15:28,080 --> 00:15:30,296
Come on, have your breakfast.

224
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:32,816
Here, wipe your hands. We're running out of time. Eat up.

225
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:34,936
Or you'll be late for school.

226
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:36,535
Sweetie, listen.

227
00:15:36,559 --> 00:15:39,536
- You can't just eat meat and skip the veggies.
- Why not?

228
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:42,256
If so, you won't be able to, you know, go.

229
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:43,495
I go just fine!

230
00:15:43,519 --> 00:15:46,174
Come on, yesterday you were straining.

231
00:15:46,198 --> 00:15:47,838
Eat up.

232
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:53,216
Sorry, I need to go.

233
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:54,375
Go ahead.

234
00:15:54,399 --> 00:15:56,120
We're almost late. Hurry!

235
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:03,536
Dad, are you done yet?

236
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:04,936
Almost!

237
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:06,816
Hurry up! I'm going to be late.

238
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:08,776
Coming!

239
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:12,336
You told me to eat my veggies, but you're taking forever in the bathroom.

240
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:15,500
It's fine. If you're late today, tell them your dad overslept.

241
00:16:15,524 --> 00:16:17,896
But the first class is yours.

242
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:18,897
No.

243
00:16:18,921 --> 00:16:20,376
I have an open class today.

244
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:21,656
I totally forgot.

245
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:23,680
Let's go!

246
00:16:24,290 --> 00:16:26,296
Your face isn't even wiped!

247
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:28,800
Are you going to school like this?

248
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:31,240
Hurry up.

249
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:44,656
- That hurts!
- Did I hurt you?

250
00:16:44,680 --> 00:16:46,976
- You don't know how to do hair at all!
- I practiced.

251
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:48,447
You call that "practiced"?

252
00:16:48,471 --> 00:16:51,400
Never mind, I'll do it myself. I'm off to school.

253
00:18:13,004 --> 00:18:14,564
Mr. Fu.

254
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:21,296
Sometimes poorly-timed comfort is nothing but salt in the wound.

255
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:22,840
I'm sorry.

256
00:18:27,604 --> 00:18:29,736
Not eating?

257
00:18:29,760 --> 00:18:31,760
Then I'll finish it all myself.

258
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:46,960
- Good evening, purser.
- Good evening, purser.

259
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:53,815
Sorry, the subscriber you dialed can not be connected for the moment,

260
00:18:53,839 --> 00:18:56,018
please redial later.

261
00:18:56,042 --> 00:18:58,742
Sorry, the subscriber you dialed can not.

262
00:19:18,987 --> 00:19:20,255
I'm home.

263
00:19:20,279 --> 00:19:21,495
You must be tired today.

264
00:19:21,519 --> 00:19:23,560
Get some rest early.

265
00:19:58,097 --> 00:20:00,016
Wait...

266
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:02,200
Right here in this courtyard.

267
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:06,560
Your old house is up there?

268
00:20:08,107 --> 00:20:09,736
It's not mine yet.

269
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:13,360
But soon, it'll be mine again.

270
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:16,296
How so?

271
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:18,136
Thanks to your generosity, Mr. Fu.

272
00:20:18,160 --> 00:20:21,096
That signing bonus was pretty decent.

273
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:22,296
Unfortunately,

274
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:26,456
this area got rezoned for a school district, so it's still a bit out of reach.

275
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:30,576
Just a few more paychecks and I should be able to get it.

276
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:32,920
Come on, let me show you.

277
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:47,456
See that window?

278
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:50,936
I lived there for 20 years.

279
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:54,616
That spot right in front of it used to have our dining table.

280
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:59,440
My dad and I would have breakfast there every morning.

281
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:09,360
What's wrong?

282
00:21:11,040 --> 00:21:12,560
Nothing.

283
00:21:18,519 --> 00:21:22,800
I'll make it back here someday.

284
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:30,505
I've said too much tonight.

285
00:21:30,529 --> 00:21:32,009
Let's go.

286
00:21:57,029 --> 00:21:59,360
Mr. Fu, I'm off.

287
00:22:00,382 --> 00:22:02,222
Ruan Si Xian.

288
00:22:03,920 --> 00:22:05,520
Yes?

289
00:22:07,533 --> 00:22:09,230
Nothing.

290
00:22:09,254 --> 00:22:10,774
Good night.

291
00:22:11,861 --> 00:22:13,341
Good night.

292
00:22:59,040 --> 00:23:05,040
[Notice Regarding the Handling of Hengshi Air Flight SH2076 Emergency Incident]

293
00:23:07,800 --> 00:23:10,056
Your mentor really is something.

294
00:23:10,080 --> 00:23:13,376
Do you remember what happened after?

295
00:23:13,400 --> 00:23:16,575
After? She became a celebrity captain, then an instructor.

296
00:23:16,599 --> 00:23:17,776
Now she's my mentor.

297
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:19,400
Why?

298
00:23:20,473 --> 00:23:21,456
Nothing.

299
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:23,336
Ruan Si Xian.

300
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:24,960
Yes?

301
00:23:26,345 --> 00:23:27,905
Nothing.

302
00:23:40,120 --> 00:23:42,736
- What...
- Manager Wang.

303
00:23:42,760 --> 00:23:45,479
I'm sorry. I was in a hurry.

304
00:23:45,503 --> 00:23:47,656
You're always charging around.

305
00:23:47,680 --> 00:23:50,176
- Where are you going?
- Manager Wang, have you heard?

306
00:23:50,200 --> 00:23:51,335
My mentor's been grounded.

307
00:23:51,359 --> 00:23:52,776
There's got to be some mistake.

308
00:23:52,800 --> 00:23:54,161
Then what are you planning to do?

309
00:23:54,185 --> 00:23:56,016
I need to talk to our group captain.

310
00:23:56,040 --> 00:23:58,200
Hold on. Wait a minute.

311
00:23:59,514 --> 00:24:00,897
Come with me.

312
00:24:00,921 --> 00:24:02,576
Come on. Sit over there.

313
00:24:02,600 --> 00:24:04,856
I'll get you some water.

314
00:24:04,880 --> 00:24:06,816
- Sit down.
- I don't have time for this.

315
00:24:06,840 --> 00:24:08,456
I have to go.

316
00:24:08,480 --> 00:24:09,735
What's the rush?

317
00:24:09,759 --> 00:24:11,616
I know exactly what's going on.

318
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:13,656
I know what you're about to say.

319
00:24:13,680 --> 00:24:19,256
That's why I pulled you aside to get you to calm down.

320
00:24:19,280 --> 00:24:21,240
Sit right there and don't move.

321
00:24:22,400 --> 00:24:25,449
The company knows what it's doing.

322
00:24:25,473 --> 00:24:27,776
This whole thing is temporary.

323
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:29,376
Why are you getting so worked up?

324
00:24:29,400 --> 00:24:31,656
But being grounded is a big deal.

325
00:24:31,680 --> 00:24:34,216
My mentor didn't do anything wrong yesterday.

326
00:24:34,240 --> 00:24:37,282
The plane landed safely, the passenger got medical care on time,

327
00:24:37,306 --> 00:24:39,136
and Mr. Fu even bought the whole crew dinner.

328
00:24:39,160 --> 00:24:41,456
I know all of that.

329
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:44,416
And if you go to your group captain, he can't do anything either.

330
00:24:44,440 --> 00:24:45,456
Fine.

331
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:46,936
Then I won't go to him.

332
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:48,496
Then I'll go straight to Mr. Fu and ask him,

333
00:24:48,520 --> 00:24:50,535
the thank-you from last night, or the penalty this morning,

334
00:24:50,559 --> 00:24:52,376
which is it?

335
00:24:52,400 --> 00:24:53,856
That won't change a thing.

336
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:55,416
This is a company decision.

337
00:24:55,440 --> 00:24:59,376
We're all on Captain Fan's side emotionally.

338
00:24:59,400 --> 00:25:02,776
But the company has its safety assessment system.

339
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:06,376
Once it's triggered, the pilot gets grounded for investigation.

340
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:09,456
But the system is not set in stone.

341
00:25:09,480 --> 00:25:11,216
It's made by humans.

342
00:25:11,240 --> 00:25:14,176
Besides, my mentor saved a life. She should be commended, not punished.

343
00:25:14,200 --> 00:25:15,696
Is Fu Ming Yu that blind to right and wrong?

344
00:25:15,720 --> 00:25:18,255
Ruan Si Xian, let me be straight with you.

345
00:25:18,279 --> 00:25:19,535
First thing this morning,

346
00:25:19,559 --> 00:25:22,656
Captain Fan herself accepted the decision.

347
00:25:22,680 --> 00:25:23,815
If you kick up a fuss right now,

348
00:25:23,839 --> 00:25:27,020
are you doing her a favor, or just making things more difficult for her?

349
00:25:31,040 --> 00:25:33,856
Sit right there and finish this glass of water.

350
00:25:33,880 --> 00:25:36,416
Think it through.

351
00:25:36,440 --> 00:25:38,480
And you're not leaving till it's empty.

352
00:26:02,480 --> 00:26:05,279
No. I totally feel this one.

353
00:26:05,303 --> 00:26:07,055
You work your tail off all day,

354
00:26:07,079 --> 00:26:09,256
and instead of a thank-you,

355
00:26:09,280 --> 00:26:11,296
they tell you to hand over your badge and leave?

356
00:26:11,320 --> 00:26:14,096
- That's just wrong.
- Right?

357
00:26:14,120 --> 00:26:16,536
To me, it's a total slap in the face.

358
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:19,976
And last night, I was like an idiot, strolling down the street with him,

359
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:22,336
pouring my heart out about buying back my house.

360
00:26:22,360 --> 00:26:23,896
I thought we were friends,

361
00:26:23,920 --> 00:26:26,295
but he's ready to put his employees at the bottom of the pile.

362
00:26:26,319 --> 00:26:28,776
Hold up. I have a question.

363
00:26:28,800 --> 00:26:32,576
Since when have you two been friends?

364
00:26:32,600 --> 00:26:34,840
Is that the point?

365
00:26:36,200 --> 00:26:39,496
You're not taking his side on this, are you?

366
00:26:39,520 --> 00:26:42,616
When have I ever taken his side?

367
00:26:42,640 --> 00:26:45,815
I'm just being objective.

368
00:26:45,839 --> 00:26:47,736
Mr. Fu's the vice president.

369
00:26:47,760 --> 00:26:50,456
Anything that lands on his desk, he's got to sign.

370
00:26:50,480 --> 00:26:54,296
That doesn't mean he's happy about every single one of them.

371
00:26:54,320 --> 00:26:57,844
Otherwise, why did he have that look on his face last night?

372
00:26:57,868 --> 00:26:59,976
Like he had something to say but couldn't?

373
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:03,536
So he grounds my mentor, and I'm supposed to feel sorry for him now?

374
00:27:03,560 --> 00:27:06,016
Wait, don't drag me into this.

375
00:27:06,040 --> 00:27:07,776
I'm innocent.

376
00:27:07,800 --> 00:27:12,336
I think the really innocent one is Ruan's mentor, Captain Fan.

377
00:27:12,360 --> 00:27:16,080
She did the right thing, yet she's the one paying for it.

378
00:27:18,640 --> 00:27:20,440
Your phone's ringing.

379
00:27:24,119 --> 00:27:25,880
It's my mentor.

380
00:27:29,457 --> 00:27:31,161
Hello, mentor?

381
00:27:31,185 --> 00:27:34,920
Ruan, you're off tomorrow. Got any plans?

382
00:27:35,560 --> 00:27:37,080
No.

383
00:27:39,595 --> 00:27:42,720
Slow down! Watch yourself!

384
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:47,336
Thanks for giving up your day off to help me with the kid.

385
00:27:47,360 --> 00:27:48,656
I owe you one.

386
00:27:48,680 --> 00:27:52,280
I didn't realize Lu Lu was already in full-time daycare.

387
00:27:54,247 --> 00:27:56,896
Well, her grandparents aren't retired yet.

388
00:27:56,920 --> 00:27:58,576
That's just how it is when both parents are pilots.

389
00:27:58,600 --> 00:28:01,016
But honestly, this might be a blessing in disguise.

390
00:28:01,040 --> 00:28:03,656
I haven't taken her out to play in forever.

391
00:28:03,680 --> 00:28:09,560
But I still don't think it's fair.

392
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:12,656
What would be fair, then?

393
00:28:12,680 --> 00:28:14,936
Didn't the patient get timely treatment?

394
00:28:14,960 --> 00:28:18,896
Yeah, but we didn't do anything wrong, and you still got penalized.

395
00:28:18,920 --> 00:28:22,696
And even if someone had to take the fall, it shouldn't all be on you.

396
00:28:22,720 --> 00:28:24,176
If not me, then who?

397
00:28:24,200 --> 00:28:26,816
I'm the captain in command.

398
00:28:26,840 --> 00:28:31,040
The day you're sitting in that seat, you'll do the same.

399
00:28:37,120 --> 00:28:41,600
You know why I recommended you to the Aviation Academy back then?

400
00:28:43,440 --> 00:28:46,536
Wasn't it because I kept pushing you until you finally gave in?

401
00:28:46,560 --> 00:28:49,496
But you still had to convince me.

402
00:28:49,520 --> 00:28:52,952
And back then, the academy only took sponsored pilots.

403
00:28:52,976 --> 00:28:55,166
Then why?

404
00:28:55,190 --> 00:29:00,376
I remember telling you every single challenge female pilots face.

405
00:29:00,400 --> 00:29:04,696
Anyone else would have weighed the pros and cons and walked.

406
00:29:04,720 --> 00:29:06,501
But you didn't.

407
00:29:06,525 --> 00:29:09,520
You came back and told me you'd made your choice.

408
00:29:10,240 --> 00:29:14,896
You'd sell your house, pay your own tuition, whatever it took.

409
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:18,736
Around that time, I'd just had the baby.

410
00:29:18,760 --> 00:29:21,582
Everyone at home wanted me to quit and be a full-time mom.

411
00:29:21,606 --> 00:29:24,296
And I was burnt out too.

412
00:29:24,320 --> 00:29:26,720
I was ready to hand in my resignation.

413
00:29:27,563 --> 00:29:29,763
But then you showed up.

414
00:29:31,619 --> 00:29:35,800
I suddenly saw myself back when I first started flying.

415
00:29:36,680 --> 00:29:40,656
That passion came flooding back.

416
00:29:40,680 --> 00:29:47,055
So in a way, I gave you a leg up, but you also gave me one.

417
00:29:47,079 --> 00:29:49,416
But when it happened, I froze.

418
00:29:49,440 --> 00:29:51,696
You didn't hesitate to save that passenger,

419
00:29:51,720 --> 00:29:54,056
and I tried to hold you back.

420
00:29:54,080 --> 00:29:58,976
We all know a bank angle over 30 degrees triggers the QAR warning.

421
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:03,856
But a steep bank with autopilot off buys the patient more time,

422
00:30:03,880 --> 00:30:05,456
so I think it's worth it.

423
00:30:05,480 --> 00:30:07,122
There's nothing to be afraid of.

424
00:30:07,146 --> 00:30:13,176
As pilots, we put our passengers' lives and safety above everything else.

425
00:30:13,200 --> 00:30:15,415
I'd do it again without hesitation.

426
00:30:15,439 --> 00:30:17,096
And I don't regret it.

427
00:30:17,120 --> 00:30:19,976
Whether you and Yu tried to persuade me or stop me,

428
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:22,116
I know you meant well.

429
00:30:22,140 --> 00:30:25,255
But sticking to the rulebook

430
00:30:25,279 --> 00:30:29,536
is exactly what you two should be doing at this stage.

431
00:30:29,560 --> 00:30:34,976
And the minute I gave that order, I already knew what was coming.

432
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:36,616
I still chose to do it.

433
00:30:36,640 --> 00:30:39,696
That means I was ready to face whatever came next.

434
00:30:39,720 --> 00:30:41,536
So don't be too hard on yourselves.

435
00:30:41,560 --> 00:30:44,677
And don't go arguing with Mr. Fu on my account.

436
00:30:44,701 --> 00:30:46,480
After all,

437
00:30:47,240 --> 00:30:50,771
this kind of call isn't his alone to make anyway.

438
00:30:50,795 --> 00:30:53,392
We saved a life.

439
00:30:53,416 --> 00:30:55,975
A kid still has her mom.

440
00:30:55,999 --> 00:30:58,376
That honestly makes me happy.

441
00:30:58,400 --> 00:30:59,880
Truly.

442
00:31:03,760 --> 00:31:05,896
Mentor

443
00:31:05,920 --> 00:31:07,640
I'm sorry.

444
00:31:08,440 --> 00:31:10,696
I have to be honest.

445
00:31:10,720 --> 00:31:14,335
I thought about going to appeal for you.

446
00:31:14,359 --> 00:31:18,176
But they said it would just make things worse.

447
00:31:18,200 --> 00:31:20,000
And.

448
00:31:20,796 --> 00:31:23,856
I backed off.

449
00:31:23,880 --> 00:31:25,295
I feel like a coward.

450
00:31:25,319 --> 00:31:29,416
Ruan, at that moment, I had all those passengers behind me

451
00:31:29,440 --> 00:31:30,976
and barely any time.

452
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:33,536
I had to decide right then and there.

453
00:31:33,560 --> 00:31:35,336
You have to remember,

454
00:31:35,360 --> 00:31:38,216
we shall see every passenger back there

455
00:31:38,240 --> 00:31:42,642
our parent, our grandparent, or our sibling.

456
00:31:42,666 --> 00:31:47,659
Maybe they're heading home, or to a reunion,

457
00:31:47,683 --> 00:31:50,056
or chasing a dream or love.

458
00:31:50,080 --> 00:31:53,576
Our job is to get them there safe and sound.

459
00:31:53,600 --> 00:31:56,400
That's our highest mission.

460
00:31:59,116 --> 00:32:01,036
I get it, mentor.

461
00:32:37,338 --> 00:32:38,795
Morning.

462
00:32:38,819 --> 00:32:41,196
Morning, Mr. Yan.

463
00:32:41,220 --> 00:32:43,220
Are you flying today?

464
00:32:46,635 --> 00:32:47,652
Jump in.

465
00:32:47,676 --> 00:32:50,757
I'm on the way to the airport base. Just passing by.

466
00:32:52,089 --> 00:32:54,968
We said we'd still be friends, right?

467
00:32:54,992 --> 00:32:56,176
And it is on my way, really.

468
00:32:56,200 --> 00:32:57,776
No, it's not that.

469
00:32:57,800 --> 00:33:01,720
I just called a taxi. It should be here soon.

470
00:33:02,640 --> 00:33:04,776
I've been watching you for a while.

471
00:33:04,800 --> 00:33:06,920
You haven't gotten one.

472
00:33:07,800 --> 00:33:12,440
Mr. Yan, it doesn't look like you're "just passing by."

473
00:33:13,719 --> 00:33:16,042
Don't call me out like that.

474
00:33:16,066 --> 00:33:18,946
Come on, get in. You don't want to be late.

475
00:33:20,287 --> 00:33:22,656
Alright then. Thanks.

476
00:33:22,680 --> 00:33:24,120
Let's go.

477
00:33:26,422 --> 00:33:27,942
Watch your head.

478
00:33:55,680 --> 00:33:57,960
If you have something to say, just say it.

479
00:34:01,569 --> 00:34:07,416
Ruan Si Xian, I never properly apologized for what happened before.

480
00:34:07,440 --> 00:34:08,776
I'm sorry.

481
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:10,336
That's in the past.

482
00:34:10,360 --> 00:34:12,776
Let's drop it.

483
00:34:12,800 --> 00:34:14,376
Just tell me what's on your mind.

484
00:34:14,400 --> 00:34:16,816
To be honest,

485
00:34:16,840 --> 00:34:23,320
did you turn me down because of Fu Ming Yu?

486
00:34:26,360 --> 00:34:27,696
Don't even bother answering.

487
00:34:27,720 --> 00:34:32,175
He's been bad-mouthing me left and right,

488
00:34:32,199 --> 00:34:36,095
making me look bad so he can swoop in himself.

489
00:34:36,119 --> 00:34:37,615
Is that all you wanted to say?

490
00:34:37,639 --> 00:34:40,575
No, there's more. I've thought it through.

491
00:34:40,599 --> 00:34:42,575
If he's going to play dirty, so will I.

492
00:34:42,599 --> 00:34:46,285
Trade dirt? I've got plenty.

493
00:34:46,309 --> 00:34:49,736
When in fourth grade, Fu Ming Yu went to the bathroom without toilet paper.

494
00:34:49,760 --> 00:34:52,336
Stuck in there for over two hours. Legs went completely numb.

495
00:34:52,360 --> 00:34:54,498
I had to bring him some toilet paper.

496
00:34:54,522 --> 00:34:57,816
I've got a ton of stories like that.

497
00:34:57,840 --> 00:34:59,535
He messed things up for me?

498
00:34:59,559 --> 00:35:01,495
Fine. Then nobody gets a free pass.

499
00:35:01,519 --> 00:35:04,416
If you want to hear more, I've got plenty of dirt on him.

500
00:35:04,440 --> 00:35:08,800
I can start from kindergarten.

501
00:35:16,280 --> 00:35:17,816
- I know.
- Like that one...

502
00:35:17,840 --> 00:35:21,340
- That smug little grin, remember?
- Yes, I do!

503
00:35:21,960 --> 00:35:23,615
I saw that too.

504
00:35:23,639 --> 00:35:24,736
Sorry.

505
00:35:24,760 --> 00:35:27,096
You didn't even open your suitcase?

506
00:35:27,120 --> 00:35:28,296
Did that really happen?

507
00:35:28,320 --> 00:35:30,136
Really. Why would I make that up?

508
00:35:30,160 --> 00:35:32,776
- Unbelievable.
- Call me later. Bye.

509
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:34,360
Bye.

510
00:35:35,860 --> 00:35:37,677
Showing up to work in person, Mr. Fu?

511
00:35:37,701 --> 00:35:39,661
Picking up a side gig as a driver now?

512
00:36:01,176 --> 00:36:03,176
He's really something else!

513
00:36:04,920 --> 00:36:06,976
Where were we?

514
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:10,336
We were talking about Captain Fan. Maintenance has done their checks.

515
00:36:10,360 --> 00:36:14,136
The landing was a bit overweight, but the aircraft's fine.

516
00:36:14,160 --> 00:36:16,936
I've gone over it back and forth with the Safety Committee,

517
00:36:16,960 --> 00:36:19,056
and the answer keeps coming back the same.

518
00:36:19,080 --> 00:36:21,640
It exceeded the QAR parameters.

519
00:36:22,320 --> 00:36:25,775
Honestly, I've always thought the system itself is flawed.

520
00:36:25,799 --> 00:36:29,776
The QAR is just a data recorder,

521
00:36:29,800 --> 00:36:34,695
but the company tightened the thresholds way beyond what's really necessary for safety,

522
00:36:34,719 --> 00:36:37,016
just to make management easier.

523
00:36:37,040 --> 00:36:39,936
Over the years, pilots flying perfectly safely still got penalized

524
00:36:39,960 --> 00:36:44,400
for exceeding the QAR parameters by a hair.

525
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:47,760
So you think it's unfair.

526
00:36:51,200 --> 00:36:54,107
It's okay, you can say it.

527
00:36:54,131 --> 00:36:56,856
I think it's more than unfair.

528
00:36:56,880 --> 00:37:00,395
The company's QAR oversight is way too strict.

529
00:37:00,419 --> 00:37:06,320
If you ask me, over compliance means nothing but lazy management.

530
00:37:10,760 --> 00:37:14,497
Zhu Dong, I'm glad to hear you say that.

531
00:37:14,521 --> 00:37:18,816
But for the company, this is a major reform we have to face.

532
00:37:18,840 --> 00:37:21,016
Reform is a big deal.

533
00:37:21,040 --> 00:37:24,656
You haven't been at Hengshi Air long. Don't stir up too much trouble.

534
00:37:24,680 --> 00:37:28,541
Spending time and energy on something pointless,

535
00:37:28,565 --> 00:37:30,480
that's what I call stirring up trouble.

536
00:37:31,125 --> 00:37:36,560
Right now, our priority is to sort out Captain Fan's matter properly.

537
00:38:45,960 --> 00:38:48,456
What are you doing here?

538
00:38:48,480 --> 00:38:50,056
Waiting for you.

539
00:38:50,080 --> 00:38:51,920
For what?

540
00:39:00,923 --> 00:39:05,483
Why were you with Yan An today?

541
00:39:11,219 --> 00:39:12,544
What?

542
00:39:13,447 --> 00:39:16,160
Why were you in his car?

543
00:39:17,362 --> 00:39:19,217
He gave me a ride.

544
00:39:19,241 --> 00:39:20,583
What?

545
00:39:20,607 --> 00:39:23,448
Do I need to report that to you?

546
00:39:24,360 --> 00:39:26,336
Why?

547
00:39:26,360 --> 00:39:28,896
I said he gave me a ride because it was on his way.

548
00:39:28,920 --> 00:39:31,680
If you've had too much to drink, go home and sleep.

549
00:39:42,800 --> 00:39:44,056
Let go.

550
00:39:44,080 --> 00:39:45,936
Are you going to tell me who I can hang out with?

551
00:39:45,960 --> 00:39:47,456
Don't you think you're crossing a line?

552
00:39:47,480 --> 00:39:49,456
You're my boss.

553
00:39:49,480 --> 00:39:52,360
Are you going to manage my life too?

554
00:39:53,846 --> 00:39:57,456
Unless you don't want to be my boss,

555
00:39:57,480 --> 00:39:59,640
but want to be my boyfriend instead?

556
00:40:01,679 --> 00:40:03,640
In your dreams.

557
00:40:31,600 --> 00:40:33,096
- Hello.
- Hello.

558
00:40:33,120 --> 00:40:34,816
I have an appointment with Mr. Fu.

559
00:40:34,840 --> 00:40:36,056
Mr. Fu is in a meeting right now.

560
00:40:36,080 --> 00:40:39,160
Would you like to wait inside?

561
00:40:45,119 --> 00:40:46,720
Please, have a seat.

562
00:40:48,400 --> 00:40:50,840
Have some water.

563
00:41:03,920 --> 00:41:05,296
The first love returned after years abroad?

564
00:41:05,320 --> 00:41:06,496
Got that booked?

565
00:41:06,520 --> 00:41:09,760
Yes, don't worry. It's all set.

566
00:41:11,199 --> 00:41:14,135
- Fu Ming Yu, Mr. Fu.
- What are you doing here?

567
00:41:14,159 --> 00:41:15,176
My new proposal.

568
00:41:15,200 --> 00:41:17,296
I've been working on it for a week.

569
00:41:17,320 --> 00:41:18,816
I guarantee you'll be satisfied.

570
00:41:18,840 --> 00:41:22,376
Mr. Fu, Instructor Fang is waiting for you at the training center.

571
00:41:22,400 --> 00:41:25,048
I'm swamped today. You might have to wait a while.

572
00:41:25,072 --> 00:41:27,480
- Let's go.
- Of course.

573
00:41:28,360 --> 00:41:33,280
How long... is "a while"?

574
00:41:36,760 --> 00:41:39,080
Merely a contractor.

575
00:41:39,833 --> 00:41:47,216
That's my story of how I became a pilot at Hengshi Air.

576
00:41:47,240 --> 00:41:50,256
I hope it helps.

577
00:41:50,280 --> 00:41:51,840
Thank you.

578
00:41:57,640 --> 00:42:02,336
Honestly, I'd love to come to Baidao University again

579
00:42:02,360 --> 00:42:06,816
to talk more about single-pilot operations and fully automated flight.

580
00:42:06,840 --> 00:42:09,216
And next time, I could bring along a colleague of mine.

581
00:42:09,240 --> 00:42:11,056
Her name is Ruan Si Xian.

582
00:42:11,080 --> 00:42:12,816
She's also a Baidao graduate.

583
00:42:12,840 --> 00:42:14,336
Your senior.

584
00:42:14,360 --> 00:42:16,896
When I first met her, I was curious.

585
00:42:16,920 --> 00:42:20,446
What kind of school produces a pilot like that?

586
00:42:20,470 --> 00:42:23,697
And after being here today, I get it.

587
00:42:23,721 --> 00:42:25,440
You're all amazing.

588
00:42:25,464 --> 00:42:30,376
I really wish I'd had the chance to spend four years at a place like this.

589
00:42:30,400 --> 00:42:35,976
There's still some time left, and I'm sure you all have questions.

590
00:42:36,000 --> 00:42:40,520
Go ahead, feel free to ask.

591
00:42:43,120 --> 00:42:44,576
Yes, the young man over there.

592
00:42:44,600 --> 00:42:46,056
Captain Yue, I'd like to ask,

593
00:42:46,080 --> 00:42:49,840
once you become a captain, does finding a partner get any easier?

594
00:42:51,840 --> 00:42:54,456
I can give you a straight answer.

595
00:42:54,480 --> 00:42:59,696
I think there's a common misconception about pilots.

596
00:42:59,720 --> 00:43:04,283
I can't speak for other airlines, but at ours, a lot of pilots are still single.

597
00:43:04,307 --> 00:43:05,936
Our circle is really small.

598
00:43:05,960 --> 00:43:07,962
We're either flying or resting.

599
00:43:07,986 --> 00:43:10,936
We don't have much time to focus on personal matters.

600
00:43:10,960 --> 00:43:12,296
- Thank you.
- What about you?

601
00:43:12,320 --> 00:43:14,400
Are you single too?

602
00:43:18,440 --> 00:43:20,416
I am.

603
00:43:20,440 --> 00:43:21,976
Still working on that one.

604
00:43:22,000 --> 00:43:23,336
Haven't cracked it yet.

605
00:43:23,360 --> 00:43:24,816
That's great!

606
00:43:24,840 --> 00:43:26,520
That's great!
